  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Eager validation",
      "items": [
        "NewWithAuthSource calls Init once, before any request, and fails with \"init auth source\" if it errors.",
        "OAuth2 fetches a first token, the static token must not be empty, and the Kubernetes token file must be readable and non-empty."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "lkctl auth mode",
      "items": [
        "--auth-mode (or LAKEKEEPER_AUTH_MODE) picks oauth2, token or k8s; oauth2 is the default.",
        "lkctl first checks the flags the mode needs and rejects an unknown mode.",
        "In oauth2 mode it fetches a token before building the auth source."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Header on every request",
      "items": [
        "AuthRoundTripper calls Header on every attempt, retries included, and keeps a header the caller already set.",
        "OAuth2 reuses its token until it expires, the static token never changes, and the Kubernetes token file is re-read each time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Bootstrap",
      "items": [
        "WithInitialBootstrap(false, …) does nothing.",
        "Otherwise construction calls Server.Info and calls Server.Bootstrap only on a server that is not bootstrapped yet; both requests carry the header.",
        "lkctl --bootstrap passes WithInitialBootstrap as an operator of user type application."
      ]
    }
  ]
